        <td><strong>&lt; 350 ms</strong></td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2>2.3 Objectives</h2>
<p>The primary technical objectives of this investigation are defined as follows:</p>
<ol>
    <li>To construct a high-fidelity Digital Twin graph abstraction representing a 30-node hierarchical hospital campus network.</li>
    <li>To engineer a hybrid FTS-LSTM + MPNN spatio-temporal model capable of predicting network anomalies 15 to 30 seconds prior to catastrophic link saturation.</li>
    <li>To implement Focal Loss ($\gamma = 2.0$) optimization to overcome extreme 98:2 telemetry class imbalance.</li>
    <li>To formulate an automated SDN remediation controller that translates predicted failure classes into OpenFlow flow-mod directives (dynamic QoS rerouting, port isolation).</li>
    <li>To build an interactive, non-AI aesthetic web NOC dashboard featuring Cytoscape.js compound ward layouts and Chart.js inspection drawers.</li>
</ol>

<h2>2.4 Problem Statement</h2>
<p>
Modern hierarchical campus networks operating in high-demand hospital environments lack predictive intelligence and automated remediation capabilities. Localized buffer bottlenecks, hardware degradation, and Spanning-Tree loops propagate silently across tiers before legacy SNMP monitoring systems raise alarms. When alerts are triggered, human network operators require tens of minutes to diagnose the root cause and execute manual CLI fixes, causing severe disruptions to critical clinical applications. There is an urgent necessity for an autonomous, spatio-temporal digital twin framework that predicts impending failures in advance and executes sub-second closed-loop SDN remediation without human delay.
</p>

<h2>2.5 Project Plan and Milestones</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Milestone 1 (Weeks 1-2):</strong> Architectural design, telemetry schema formulation, and literature review.</li>
    <li><strong>Milestone 2 (Weeks 3-4):</strong> 30-node campus topology modeling and physics-based synthetic failure dataset generation.</li>
    <li><strong>Milestone 3 (Weeks 5-6):</strong> FTS-LSTM and MPNN model architecture implementation and Focal Loss tuning.</li>
    <li><strong>Milestone 4 (Weeks 7-8):</strong> OpenFlow SDN remediation engine development and intent synthesis logic.</li>
    <li><strong>Milestone 5 (Weeks 9-10):</strong> Web NOC dashboard engineering (Cytoscape + Chart.js) and end-to-end closed-loop validation.</li>
</ul>

