<h1>CHAPTER 6<br>PROJECT DEMONSTRATION</h1>
<br>

<h2>6.1 User Interface Description</h2>
<p>
The project features an enterprise-grade Network Operations Center (NOC) dashboard accessible at <code>http://127.0.0.1:5000</code>. Key interface components include:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Left Sidebar:</strong> Displays live network health counters (Total Active Nodes: 30, Issues Detected), an interactive <em>Fault Simulation Control Panel</em>, and predicted issue alert cards.</li>
    <li><strong>Center Topology Canvas:</strong> Renders the 30-node topology using Cytoscape.js with the <code>fcose</code> compound spring layout. Switches are cleanly organized inside labeled ward bounding boxes (Datacenter, ICU, ER, etc.) with zero overlapping or clutter.</li>
    <li><strong>Telemetry Inspection Drawer:</strong> Clicking on any node circle opens a Bootstrap offcanvas drawer rendering two real-time Chart.js graphs displaying 15-step degradation curves for Bandwidth Load, Queue Depth, Packet Drops, and CRC Errors.</li>
    <li><strong>Activity Console:</strong> Displays real-time audit logs of autonomous SDN OpenFlow flow-mod deployments.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.2 Step-by-Step Demonstration Flow</h2>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Baseline Verification:</strong> The dashboard loads with all 30 nodes operating within nominal thresholds (15-30% utilization).</li>
    <li><strong>Anomaly Injection:</strong> Using the Fault Simulation Panel, the user selects <em>Node 8</em>, selects <em>"Broadcast Storm"</em>, and clicks <em>"Simulate Fault"</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Predictive Detection:</strong> Within one polling cycle, the AI identifies the anomaly, turns Node 8 <strong>Red</strong>, and generates an actionable alert card: <em>"Spanning-Tree Protocol failure detected. Implement MAC-level port isolation."</em></li>
    <li><strong>Telemetry Inspection:</strong> Clicking Node 8 slides out the inspection drawer, displaying the packet drop rate spiking to 120 pps.</li>
    <li><strong>Autonomous Remediation:</strong> Clicking <em>"Apply Fix"</em> triggers the SDN controller, which pushes the OpenFlow drop rule. The activity console logs the deployment, and Node 8 immediately restores to <strong>Green</strong>.</li>
</ol>

